        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fd65275d31254d258c55c6cfcc79b763",
      "statement": "Inbound task_request execution is gated in fixed order before any task is created or callback invoked: the sender must be a friend in accepted state (FRIEND_NOT_FOUND otherwise), the granted permission matrix must allow the requested action/resource (PERMISSION_DENIED), and the per-friend/action token-bucket rate limiter must pass (RATE_LIMITED).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L283-L295",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b742568e7ccdbc54c40b28b3e3d5d8d5e6940a06ec490871c7617bd241743d7f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_af83c4c9bd334642b1251e0f9ca9b8f6",
      "statement": "on_task(task_id, payload) drives the executor reply in three ways: a returned dict completes synchronously through the legal submitted -> accepted -> completed transitions and is answered with a task_result {state: completed, detail}; returning None moves the task to accepted then working and replies task_accept, with the final result pushed later as a task_result envelope; a raised callback marks the task failed and answers task_result {state: failed, detail.error}, so executor exceptions never leak to the sender. Incoming task_result envelopes are recorded into the local task registry by task_id.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/server.py#L296-L325",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:10dab5084214eb0c8e1f042bdb6d661b49029cd93f130bd89ce04d350da12f4e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_51cb97f72424493180ae71a7779ffed1",
      "statement": "Marketplace bookings route through the same on_task boundary as delegated tasks: _on_service_book refuses when marketplace_policy.auto_accept is false (PERMISSION_DENIED); otherwise it creates a task with action booking:reserve, invokes on_task so the booking lands in the business backend (e.g. a CalDAV calendar write in demo_marketplace), merges the returned dict into the booking, and answers a completed task_result with an MKT-<ts> task id; a raising callback becomes a TASK_ERROR envelope. Marketplace senders additionally face a blocklist check and a stricter dedicated token bucket.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://demo_marketplace.py#L32-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:553bfbdb550cc126371fbc1657c092098a33f15ba57d5d4c991d04f05881d4a1:"
