    {
      "id": "claim_65301a8a6cd7440cb60a3c6a11ce1840",
      "statement": "The transport layer is minimal by design — a transport only needs send(envelope, url) returning the reply envelope or None for fire-and-forget — and only MemoryTransport (in-process delivery to the peer router; tests and two agents in one process) and HttpTransport (HTTPS POST of the envelope JSON via a requests.Session) are implemented. Matrix and Email adapters are documented in ARQUITECTURA section 9 (signed envelopes as Matrix room events or email attachments), not code.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/ARQUITECTURA.md#L261-L271",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:71e720097ac37dad120c870d081356ba069a614cc62437ba2b0b43de4af874e0:"
