    {
      "id": "claim_6086220d477f4f3f9a578f17f3e6fbd0",
      "statement": "Routing-level containment at the message boundary: handle_message verifies every envelope (round-trip serialization, sender public-key resolution, signature plus anti-replay nonces), audits each accepted or rejected message, and converts any HAAPError into a signed error envelope carrying a stable error_code and no internal detail, so verification and handler exceptions never escape the router as raw errors.",
